  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oshkosh Defense has $477M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Oshkosh Defense received 3,993 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $119K and obligations down 67.8% year over year. Historical fiscal-year obligations show larger recent totals: FY21 $2.2B, FY22 $1.6B, FY23 $2B, FY24 $1.3B, and FY25 $1.5B. The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $477M so far in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration is also listed among top buyers, with a value of $243. Truck Trailer Manufacturing is the largest market for Oshkosh Defense in FY2026 to date, with $333M in obligations. Other notable markets include Hardware Manufacturing $26.2M, Motor Vehicle Body Manufacturing $21.4M, Heavy Duty Truck Manufacturing $19.6M, and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing $16.9M. Smaller technical and parts markets include Other Engine Equipment Manufacturing $16.6M, Tire Manufacturing (except Retreading) $9.4M, Small Arms, Ordnance, and Ordnance Accessories Manufacturing $5.7M, Motor Vehicle Transmission and Power Train Parts Manufacturing $4.6M, and Engineering Services $4.5M.",
